{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_0173XV62VNe8ZdaNYfp6iyts","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem:** go-unix-utils is a specification-driven pipeline that regenerates Unix utilities in Go, verified via differential testing against GNU reference binaries. The goal is to stress-test the mage-claude-orchestrator code generation system.\n\n**Architecture:** Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). `cmd/` holds per-utility Go implementations, `pkg/` provides shared libraries (sys, format, testutils), `magefiles/` orchestrates builds and generation, `docs/` holds specs.\n\n**Current state:** Releases 00.0 through 05.3 have specs implemented. The most recent commit (fb24484) implements `cmd/md5sum`, `cmd/sha1sum`, `cmd/sha256sum`, `cmd/sha512sum` — the rel05.4 checksum quartet. Per the analysis, code status for all four is \"not started\" (likely stale since the commit exists). Per P2, implementation and tests are split into separate tasks, so differential tests remain.\n\n**Current release:** rel05.4 — Batch 5.4 checksum quartet. Implementation done (task 371). Tests needed.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nTask 371 implemented all four checksum utilities. Following P2 (split implementation and tests), the next task is differential tests for the quartet. All four share an identical test pattern (hash stdin/files, `--check` mode, `--tag` mode), so they fit comfortably in one test task within the 250-line budget.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"Differential tests for cmd/md5sum, cmd/sha1sum, cmd/sha256sum, cmd/sha512sum (rel05.4)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-05.4.yaml (test cases for all four checksum utilities)\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd016-checksums.yaml (requirements for md5sum, sha1sum, sha256sum, sha512sum)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel05.4-uc001-md5sum.yaml (use case for md5sum)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel05.4-uc002-sha1sum.yaml (use case for sha1sum)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel05.4-uc003-sha256sum.yaml (use case for sha256sum)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel05.4-uc004-sha512sum.yaml (use case for sha512sum)\n      - cmd/md5sum/main.go (implementation to verify)\n      - cmd/sha1sum/main.go (implementation to verify)\n      - cmd/sha256sum/main.go (implementation to verify)\n      - cmd/sha512sum/main.go (implementation to verify)\n      - pkg/testutils/difftest.go (DiffTest struct and RunDiffTests harness)\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (shared_protocols section -- differential testing pattern and graceful skip)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/md5sum/md5sum_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Differential tests for md5sum against gmd5sum\n      - path: cmd/sha1sum/sha1sum_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Differential tests for sha1sum against gsha1sum\n      - path: cmd/sha256sum/sha256sum_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Differential tests for sha256sum against gsha256sum\n      - path: cmd/sha512sum/sha512sum_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Differential tests for sha512sum against gsha512sum\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: |\n          Write differential tests for cmd/md5sum covering stdin hashing, file argument hashing,\n          multiple file arguments, --check mode (valid and corrupt), --tag mode (BSD-style output),\n          --binary and --text flags, and missing file error handling. Reference binary is gmd5sum.\n      - id: R2\n        text: |\n          Write differential tests for cmd/sha1sum with the same test matrix as R1.\n          Reference binary is gsha1sum.\n      - id: R3\n        text: |\n          Write differential tests for cmd/sha256sum with the same test matrix as R1.\n          Reference binary is gsha256sum.\n      - id: R4\n        text: |\n          Write differential tests for cmd/sha512sum with the same test matrix as R1.\n          Reference binary is gsha512sum.\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: |\n          Follow the project's shared differential testing protocol: use testutils.BuildBinary\n          to compile the Go binary, exec.LookPath for the reference binary, t.Skip if reference\n          not found, and testutils.RunDiffTests to compare stdout, stderr, and exit code.\n      - id: D2\n        text: |\n          All four test files follow an identical structure -- define a TestDiff function with\n          a []testutils.DiffTest slice. Vary only the reference binary name (gmd5sum, gsha1sum,\n          gsha256sum, gsha512sum) and the test case expected outputs. Do NOT abstract a shared\n          helper across the four files; each file is self-contained.\n      - id: D3\n        text: |\n          For --check mode tests, create temporary checksum files in t.TempDir() using the\n          reference binary's output format. Test both valid checksums and deliberately corrupted\n          checksums to verify exit code 1 and warning output.\n      - id: D4\n        text: |\n          Set LC_ALL=C in the Env field of every DiffTest to ensure consistent error messages\n          and output between Go and GNU binaries.\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go test ./cmd/md5sum/ passes with gmd5sum as reference binary\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go test ./cmd/sha1sum/ passes with gsha1sum as reference binary\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"go test ./cmd/sha256sum/ passes with gsha256sum as reference binary\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"go test ./cmd/sha512sum/ passes with gsha512sum as reference binary\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"Each test file gracefully skips (t.Skip) when the reference binary is not in PATH\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"Each test file covers at minimum: stdin input, single file, multiple files, --check valid, --check corrupt, --tag, missing file error\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":27604,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":27604},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c0685b60-836d-4d19-90bc-7b39e6d07623","uuid":"e0cefbe9-85d6-47d1-8bab-ea9423f9b23e"}
